  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Define the functions $c(x)=\\dfrac{e^x+e^{-x}}{2}$ and $s(x)=\\dfrac{e^x-e^{-x}}{2}$. Show that the following are true.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$c(x)+s(x)=e^x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$c(x)+s(x)=e^x$ because the $e^{-x}$ terms cancel.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*} c(x)+s(x)&=\\frac{(e^x+e^{-x})+(e^x-e^{-x})}{2}\\\\ c(x)+s(x)&=\\frac{2e^x}{2}\\\\ c(x)+s(x)&=e^x.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$c(x)-s(x)=e^{-x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$c(x)-s(x)=e^{-x}$ because the $e^x$ terms cancel.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*} c(x)-s(x)&=\\frac{(e^x+e^{-x})-(e^x-e^{-x})}{2}\\\\ c(x)-s(x)&=\\frac{2e^{-x}}{2}\\\\ c(x)-s(x)&=e^{-x}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$c'(x)=s(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$c'(x)=\\dfrac{e^x-e^{-x}}{2}=s(x)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*} c'(x)&=\\frac12\\left(\\frac{d}{dx}e^x+\\frac{d}{dx}e^{-x}\\right)\\\\ c'(x)&=\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}{2}\\\\ c'(x)&=s(x).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 17
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$s'(x)=c(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$s'(x)=\\dfrac{e^x+e^{-x}}{2}=c(x)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*} s'(x)&=\\frac12\\left(\\frac{d}{dx}e^x-\\frac{d}{dx}e^{-x}\\right)\\\\ s'(x)&=\\frac{e^x+e^{-x}}{2}\\\\ s'(x)&=c(x).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 17
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q12-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$s(2x)=2s(x)c(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2s(x)c(x)=s(2x)$.\n\nThe product of the two numerators is a difference of squares.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*} 2s(x)c(x)&=2\\left(\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{e^x+e^{-x}}{2}\\right)\\\\ 2s(x)c(x)&=\\frac{(e^x)^2-(e^{-x})^2}{2}\\\\ 2s(x)c(x)&=\\frac{e^{2x}-e^{-2x}}{2}\\\\ 2s(x)c(x)&=s(2x).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q12-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$c(2x)=s^2(x)+c^2(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$s^2(x)+c^2(x)=c(2x)$.\n\nThe cross terms cancel when the squares are added.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*} s^2(x)+c^2(x)&=\\frac{(e^x-e^{-x})^2+(e^x+e^{-x})^2}{4}\\\\ s^2(x)+c^2(x)&=\\frac{2(e^x)^2+2(e^{-x})^2}{4}\\\\ s^2(x)+c^2(x)&=\\frac{e^{2x}+e^{-2x}}{2}\\\\ s^2(x)+c^2(x)&=c(2x).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q12-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$c^2(x)-s^2(x)=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$c^2(x)-s^2(x)=1$.\n\nFactor the difference of squares and use (a) and (b).",
          "worked": "Factor the difference of squares, then use (a) and (b).\n\n$$\\begin{align*} c^2(x)-s^2(x)&=(c(x)+s(x))(c(x)-s(x))\\\\ c^2(x)-s^2(x)&=e^xe^{-x}\\\\ c^2(x)-s^2(x)&=1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q12-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$c(2x)=2s^2(x)+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$c(2x)=2s^2(x)+1$.\n\nUse (g) to replace $c^2(x)$ in (f).",
          "worked": "From (g), $c^2(x)=1+s^2(x)$. Substitute in (f).\n\n$$\\begin{align*} c(2x)&=s^2(x)+c^2(x)\\\\ c(2x)&=s^2(x)+(1+s^2(x))\\\\ c(2x)&=2s^2(x)+1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q12-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$s(x+y)=s(x)c(y)+c(x)s(y)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$s(x+y)=s(x)c(y)+c(x)s(y)$.\n\nUse (a) and (b) to expand the two exponential products in $2s(x+y)$.",
          "worked": "Write $e^{x+y}=e^xe^y$ and $e^{-(x+y)}=e^{-x}e^{-y}$. By (a) and (b),\n\n$$\\begin{align*} 2s(x+y)&=e^xe^y-e^{-x}e^{-y}\\\\ 2s(x+y)&=(c(x)+s(x))(c(y)+s(y))\\\\ &\\quad -(c(x)-s(x))(c(y)-s(y))\\\\ 2s(x+y)&=2s(x)c(y)+2c(x)s(y)\\\\ s(x+y)&=s(x)c(y)+c(x)s(y).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q12-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$c(x+y)=c(x)c(y)+s(x)s(y)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$c(x+y)=c(x)c(y)+s(x)s(y)$.\n\nUse (a) and (b) to expand the two exponential products in $2c(x+y)$.",
          "worked": "Write $e^{x+y}=e^xe^y$ and $e^{-(x+y)}=e^{-x}e^{-y}$. By (a) and (b),\n\n$$\\begin{align*} 2c(x+y)&=e^xe^y+e^{-x}e^{-y}\\\\ 2c(x+y)&=(c(x)+s(x))(c(y)+s(y))\\\\ &\\quad +(c(x)-s(x))(c(y)-s(y))\\\\ 2c(x+y)&=2c(x)c(y)+2s(x)s(y)\\\\ c(x+y)&=c(x)c(y)+s(x)s(y).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
